id: bouncy
name: Bouncy
kind: battlefield
envQuality: true
groundCollision: halves
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Ground that gives. Half the Collision Damage from hitting it, and you bounce up to its
  Hardness Rank in Squares.
text: >
  Bouncy: If you would Collide with this Square, halve the amount of Collision Damage you
  would receive and then you may move a number of Squares in any direction up to the
  Hardness Rank of this Square.

---

# The Square's own Rubbery, and written to read the same way: halve the Collision Damage,
# then move. Where Rubbery throws you straight away from the Feature, this lets you pick a
# direction - you land on it rather than into it.
#
# --- The halving ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `groundCollision: halves`, read by the collision window in its Ground Collision branch
# and nowhere else. "If you would Collide with this Square" is the Square, and a Feature
# standing on a Bouncy Square is not bouncy.
#
# Folded in with every other halving and the Launching doubling, so it is one multiply and
# one rounding - which is the rule that keeps 7 at 7 when something doubles it and
# something else halves it.
#
# --- The movement --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "You may move a number of Squares in any direction up to the Hardness Rank of this
# Square." Squares, a direction and a choice: three things this system has none of. Said on
# the card and done by the table, the same as Rubbery's.
#
# No statements. Everything here is a collision, and a collision is an event.
